{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.transy.edu/employment-opportunities/#op-709721-assistant-director-of-financial-aid": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "« Openings at Transylvania University Assistant Director of Financial Aid Location: Lexington, Kentucky, United States Full-time The Assistant Director of Financial Aid plays an integral role in the administration and delivery of federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs at Transylvania University. Working under the direction of the Director of Financial Aid, this position is responsible for managing assigned financial aid programs and processes while ensuring students receive accurate, timely, and compliant financial aid assistance. The Assistant Director works directly with students and families throughout the financial aid process and contributes to the successful execution of annual financial aid cycles for both new and returning students. This position has primary responsibility for the administration of Veterans Affairs (VA) educational benefits, alternative/private loans, outside scholarships, state grant programs, and assigned federal loan processes. The Assistant Director also supports the overall operations of the Financial Aid Office through financial aid packaging, file and document management, federal loan processing, and coordination with other University offices. The position requires strong attention to detail, sound judgment, and the ability to evaluate how changes to a student's enrollment, housing, or other financial resources affect overall financial aid eligibility. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Package financial aid for new and returning students in accordance with federal, state, institutional, and University policies Review and update student housing status and make appropriate adjustments to financial aid eligibility and awards Award outside scholarships and evaluate the impact of additional financial resources on existing federal, state, and institutional financial aid Administer and award Veterans Affairs (VA) educational benefits for eligible students in accordance with applicable requirements and University procedures Serve as a resource for students and families regarding the coordination of VA educational benefits with other forms of financial aid Certify and process alternative/private loan applications and ensure loan amounts are within applicable student eligibility and cost of attendance limits Utilize the U.S. Department of Education's Common Origination and Disbursement (COD) system to monitor and assist with federal student loan processing Review federal loan records to help ensure students have completed applicable loan requirements prior to disbursement Identify and assist in resolving outstanding federal loan requirements or discrepancies Assist students with federal student loan exit counseling requirements and provide guidance regarding completion of required processes Administer assigned state grant programs and ensure eligible students are awarded accurately and timely Monitor student eligibility for state financial aid programs and make necessary award adjustments Complete required reporting and reconciliation of state grant funds Maintain accurate and organized physical and electronic financial aid files in accordance with institutional policies and applicable record-retention requirements Protect the confidentiality and security of student financial information in accordance with FERPA and University policies Support efforts to maintain consistent and efficient electronic document and file-management processes Counsel students and families regarding financial aid eligibility, awards, loan requirements, and financial aid processes Respond to student and family questions in a timely, accurate, and professional manner Assist students in understanding financial aid requirements, outstanding documentation, and changes to their financial aid packages Collaborate with the Director and other Financial Aid staff to ensure timely completion of annual processing cycles and office priorities As a member of the Enrollment Management team, work collaboratively with other University offices, including Admissions, Student Accounts/Billing, Registrar, and other campus partners, to resolve student financial aid issues Maintain current knowledge of federal, state, institutional, and University financial aid policies and procedures Perform other duties related to the administration of financial aid as assigned Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution Experience in financial aid, student financial services, higher education, or a related field Working knowledge of financial aid principles, regulations, and processes Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accuracy while managing multiple responsibilities Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to prioritize work under established deadlines Ability to interpret policies and apply them consistently to individual student circumstances Strong written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated commitment to providing excellent service to students and families Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive student and financial information with professionalism Preferred Qualifications Four or more years of experience in financial aid administration or a related higher education setting Experience administering federal, state, institutional, or private financial aid programs Experience with Veterans Affairs educational benefits Experience with alternative/private education loan certification Experience with state grant administration, reporting, or reconciliation Experience using the U.S. Department of Education's COD system Experience with financial aid systems such as PowerFAIDS, Ellucian, Technolutions Slate or similar student information systems Experience at a small, private, tuition-driven institution Working Conditions and Physical Requirements Standard office environment with extended screen time Regular interaction with students, families, University staff, and external agencies Occasional evening or weekend hours during peak processing periods, enrollment events, or other University activities Hybrid work arrangements may be available in accordance with University policy and at the discretion of supervisor Apply for this position « Openings at Transylvania University"
    },
    "https://www.transy.edu/employment-opportunities/#op-663725-assistant-mens-and-womens-swimmingdiving-coach": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's and Women's Swimming/Diving Coach",
      "description": "« Openings at Transylvania University Assistant Men's and Women's Swimming/Diving Coach Location: Lexington, Kentucky, United States Full-time Transylvania University invites applications for the full-time position of Assistant Men's and Women's Swimming/Diving Coach. Transylvania, founded in 1780, is the nation's 16th oldest institution of higher learning and is consistently ranked in national publications as one of the top liberal arts colleges in the country. Transylvania is located blocks from downtown Lexington, KY, in central Kentucky. Transylvania is a proud member of NCAA Division III. The Assistant Men's and Women's Swimming/Diving Coach will assist the head coach in the management and coaching of an NCAA Division III swimming and diving program. This includes, but is not limited to, assisting with operations management (e.g., program development, schedule, camps/swim lessons, marketing, and public relations), recruiting, assist with office needs, practice plans, and other secondary duties as assigned. This position requires frequent travel; work in the evenings, on weekends and holidays. Secondary duties will include event management/sports information. This is a full-time nine-month appointment. Candidates must have a bachelor's degree and either collegiate playing experience or coaching and effective communication/organizational skills. In addition, candidates should have an athletics philosophy compatible with a Division III liberal arts college with highly selective academic standards. We will continue to accept resumes until the position is filled. Qualified candidates may submit their cover letter and resume by following the staff job openings link at www.transy.edu/jobs. Please write your cover letter to the attention of Dave Doolin, Head Men's and Women's Swimming/Diving Coach. Transylvania University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to enhancing the diversity of the university community. In support of this goal, we seek qualified candidates with a wide range of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We embrace diversity and encourage all who are interested to apply. Apply for this position « Openings at Transylvania University"
    },
    "https://www.transy.edu/employment-opportunities/#op-707588-assistant-professor-of-chemistry": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "« Openings at Transylvania University Assistant Professor of Chemistry Location: Lexington, Kentucky, United States Full-time Application closes: Oct 22, 2026 Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Biochemistry) Transylvania University (www.transy.edu) invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track position in Chemistry, beginning August 25, 2027. The chemistry program, with an emphasis on laboratory experiences, prepares students for a wide range of careers including biochemistry, chemical engineering, environmental science, materials science, medicine and other health care areas. Students learn to become skilled problem solvers and develop a strong foundation in all areas of chemistry. The program also supports students from a wide range of other programs, such as biology, neuroscience, and health and exercise science. Why Join Transylvania University? Founded in 1780, Transylvania University is one of the nation’s oldest institutions. Ranked in the Top 100 Best Liberal Arts colleges for 2025 by Niche, we’re a vibrant campus in the heart of Lexington, Kentucky full of curious minds, creative energy, and people who genuinely love what they do. We are mentors and community builders who help shape the next generation of thinkers, creators and leaders. We cultivate independent thinking, open-mindedness, creative expression and commitment to lifelong learning and social responsibility in a diverse world. With approximately 1,000 students, Transylvania is a student-centered institution with small class sizes. We offer additional opportunities for travel and team-taught courses, and a focus on experiential learning. Who Are We Looking For? Eligible candidates will have a Ph.D. by the start date. The successful candidate will have expertise in Biochemistry or Bioorganic Chemistry, a commitment to teaching, value interdisciplinary dialogue, and work collaboratively with other faculty. The teaching load consists of two classes with laboratory sections per regular term and a single class during May term (2-2-1). Responsibilities include: Teach (1) Biochemistry course, currently offered each regular term, and (2) the two-semester sequence of either Organic Chemistry (preferred) or General Chemistry. Occasional contributions to First-Year programming and service as an academic adviser. Other responsibilities include academic scholarship/professional activity, preferably involving undergraduate students, and service to the university through various committee appointments. How Do You Apply? Qualified candidates should submit a single PDF including: A cover letter that describes how you envision engaging Transylvania students in your teaching and research Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research philosophy that would include undergraduates in a liberal arts setting Unofficial graduate transcripts List of at least three professional references The successful candidate will be asked to provide official graduate transcripts and be subject to a background check. Send questions specific to this search to Dr. Kyle Schnitzenbaumer, search committee chair, at kschnitzenbaumer@transy.edu. Please apply by the application deadline of Friday, October 23, 2026. Transylvania University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to enhancing the diversity of the university community. In support of this goal, we embrace diversity and encourage applications from qualified candidates with a wide range of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. Application closes: Oct 22, 2026 Apply for this position « Openings at Transylvania University"
    },
    "https://www.transy.edu/employment-opportunities/#op-703829-assistant-womens-lacrosse-coach": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach",
      "description": "« Openings at Transylvania University Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach Location: Lexington, Kentucky, United States Full-time Transylvania University invites applications for the full-time position of Assistant Women’s Soccer Coach. Transylvania, founded in 1780, is the nation’s 16th oldest institution of higher learning and is consistently ranked in national publications as one of the top liberal arts colleges in the country. Transylvania is located blocks from downtown Lexington in central Kentucky. Transylvania is a proud member of NCAA Division III. The Assistant Women’s Lacrosse Coach will assist the head coach in the management and coaching of an NCAA Division III soccer program. This includes, but is not limited to, assisting with operations management (e.g., program development, schedule, camps, marketing, and public relations), recruiting, assisting with office needs, overseeing and planning the development of the offensive and defensive systems and other secondary duties as assigned. This position requires frequent travel; work in the evenings, on weekends and holidays. Secondary duties will include event management/sports information. This is a full-time nine-month appointment. Candidates must have a bachelor's degree and either collegiate playing experience or coaching and effective communication/organizational skills. In addition, candidates should have an athletics philosophy compatible with a Division III liberal arts college with highly selective academic standards. Please apply by August 31, 2026; however, we will continue to accept resumes until the position is filled. Qualified candidates may submit their cover letter and resume by following the staff job openings link at www.transy.edu/jobs. Please write your cover letter to the attention of Bri McCulley, Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach. Transylvania University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to enhancing the diversity of the university community. In support of this goal, we seek qualified candidates with a wide range of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We embrace diversity and encourage all who are interested to apply. Apply for this position « Openings at Transylvania University"
    },
    "https://www.transy.edu/employment-opportunities/#op-709279-human-resources-manager": {
      "title": "Human Resources Manager",
      "description": "« Openings at Transylvania University Human Resources Manager Location: Lexington, Kentucky, United States Full-time Application closes: Oct 18, 2026 Human Resources Manager - Payroll (Staff) Founded in 1780, Transylvania University is one of the nation’s oldest institutions, but don’t let our age fool you. Ranked in the Top 100 Best Liberal Arts colleges for 2025 by Niche, we’re a vibrant campus in the heart of Lexington, Kentucky full of curious minds, creative energy, and people who genuinely love what they do. We are mentors and community builders who help shape the next generation of thinkers, creators and leaders. At Transylvania, we believe our people are our greatest strength. We seek enthusiasm, initiative, and a commitment to excellence to helping create a campus environment where students, faculty and staff thrive. As a member of our community, you’ll work alongside dedicated colleagues who value collaboration, independent thinking and shared success. We invite applications for this opportunity to not only belong but belong to Team Transy! Position Title: Human Resources Manager Work Location: Lexington, KY Department: Department of Human Resources Employee Type: Full Time Position Classification (FLSA): Exempt Position Type: Staff Required License/Registration/Certification: None Shift: M-F 8:00am – 5:00pm. Additional hours required as workload demands. Posting Open Date: 10/7/2026 Posting Close Date: 10/19/2026 Overview Manage and coordinate a broad range of human resources functions in support of faculty, staff, and administrative operations. Serve as a subject matter expert and operational lead across key HR functional areas including payroll, employee relations, talent acquisition, benefits administration, HR compliance, and workforce development; and performs other duties as required. Primary Responsibilities Include: Oversees payroll operations to ensure accurate and timely processing for all faculty, staff, and student employees. Serves as the primary liaison between HR and Payroll, coordinating resolution of discrepancies, retroactive payments, and complex payroll issues. Partners with Finance to reconcile payroll data, support budget planning, and ensure alignment between HRIS and financial systems. Processes and tracks leave requests (FMLA, ADA, personal leave) in compliance with applicable law. Monitors and ensures university payroll practices comply with applicable federal, state, and local employment laws and regulations. Maintains accuracy and integrity of employee data within the university's HRIS platform. Identifies and implements improvements to payroll systems, workflows, and processes. Coordinates and facilitates employee training including new hire orientation, compliance training, and professional development programs. Assesses department-level training needs and connects employees and supervisors with relevant development resources. Generates HR reports and workforce analytics to support data-driven decision-making. Education and Experience EDUCATION: Graduate of a college or university with a bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Organizational Development or related field. EXPERIENCE: Six years of progressive experience in human resources, project coordinator, operations and/or related experience. PHR, SPHR, SHRM-CP, or SHRM-SCP certification preferred. Demonstrated experience in a complex, multi-unit organization. Experience in a higher education environment preferred. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. An Equal Opportunity Employer M/F/D/V Application closes: Oct 18, 2026 Apply for this position « Openings at Transylvania University"
    },
    "https://www.transy.edu/employment-opportunities/#op-709795-maintenance-tech-ii": {
      "title": "Maintenance Tech II",
      "description": "« Openings at Transylvania University Maintenance Tech II Location: Lexington, Kentucky, United States Full-time Essential Duties: Performs journeyman level troubleshooting and repair of building distribution systems to include Heating, Ventilation, Air Conditioning, Plumbing Systems and piping, heat exchangers, air handlers, and pneumatic and digital controls, performs required repairs through replacement of inoperative parts or adjustments of controls and blowers, and providing an estimate of repair and/or replacement of costs. Performs HVAC, Electrical and Plumbing system inspections and manufacturer-recommended preventive maintenance. Has knowledge of, can interpret and apply state and local electric and plumbing code to day to day operations Performs Plumbing system inspections and manufacturer-recommended preventive maintenance. Repairs and rebuilds plumbing fixtures to include faucets, commodes, sinks and showers. Makes recommendations and installs new plumbing fixtures to include faucets, commodes, sinks, urinals, water fountains, bottle filling stations and irrigation systems. Understands plumbing system infrastructure design and construction. Ability to read and understand plumbing, piping, electrical wiring diagrams, blueprints and specifications. Performs major component replacement work in conjunction with Maintenance Mechanic personnel on pumps, valves and other plumbing and mechanical fittings. Performs seasonal overhauls on plumbing, HVAC and mechanical systems. Contributes to efficient and effective HVAC operations by recommending the quantity and type of materials that should be ordered and stocked for use in heating, ventilation and air conditioning systems. Works with contracted heating, ventilation, and air conditioning services to ensure specified results thus minimizing future operational problems by observing (spot checking) the work performed and advising management when contract services fail to meet specifications. Helps to assure that HVAC systems operate in the intended manner to use energy efficiently by programming system parameters to meet objectives, adjusting set points, monitoring the network, and calibrating instrumentation, metering valves, dampers, actuators, controllers as required. Additional skills required for electrical focus: Installation: Install wiring, conduits, outlets, fixtures, switches, and control systems for new constructions or renovations. Maintenance: Perform general upkeep and preventive maintenance on electrical systems and components. Repair & Troubleshooting: Diagnose and fix electrical problems using testing equipment, repairing or replacing faulty wiring, equipment, or fixtures. Safety & Code Compliance: Adhere strictly to the National Electrical Code (NEC), state, and local building codes, and safety procedures. System Design: Read and interpret blueprints, technical diagrams, and schematics to plan electrical layouts. Inspection: Inspect electrical components like transformers, circuit breakers, and generators to ensure proper function. Documentation: Maintain records of repairs, modifications, and materials. Secondary Duties: Ability to use hand and power tools applicable to trade. Knowledgeable of rules and regulations of refrigerant recovery. Contributes to the overall success of the Mechanical Maintenance Department by performing other essential duties and responsibilities as assigned. Apply for this position « Openings at Transylvania University"
    },
    "https://www.transy.edu/employment-opportunities/#op-590976-peace-officer-department-of-public-safety-ftpt": {
      "title": "Peace Officer (Department of Public Safety) FT/PT",
      "description": "« Openings at Transylvania University Peace Officer (Department of Public Safety) FT/PT Location: Lexington, Kentucky, United States Full-time Overview Transylvania University invites applications for the position of Peace Officer. The Peace Officer performs safety, loss prevention, parking, and traffic control duties within an assigned area of the University campus, conducting regular vehicular and foot patrols and responding to emergency situations as appropriate. Job Skills/Requirements Duties include enforcing University parking and traffic regulations, providing directions and information, and rendering assistance to students, faculty, staff, and visitors to campus. The primary responsibility of a Peace Officer is to maintain a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, and the public, as well as all property on the Transylvania University campus. The ideal candidate will promote a positive image of the University and contribute to the overall success of the Department of Public Safety by enforcing all laws of the Commonwealth, including policies and procedures set forth by the University. The work hours for this position will be primarily 3rd shift and will require availability for weekend shifts. The position requires a high school education and one year of experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Applicants must be at least 21 years of age, as required by law to be sworn in for this position. Preference will be given to candidates with prior experience working for a law enforcement agency. Candidates must be able to obtain a Commission as a Special Local Peace Officer with the Kentucky Law Enforcement Council. A valid driver's license is also required. KLEC certification would be a plus. Transylvania University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to enhancing the diversity of the University community. In support of this goal, we seek qualified candidates with a wide range of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences. We embrace diversity and encourage all who are interested to apply. Education Requirements High School Diploma Additional Information/Benefits Benefits: Medical Insurance Life Insurance Dental Insurance Vision Insurance Paid Vacation Paid Sick Days Paid Holidays Short-Term Disability Long-Term Disability 401(k)/403(b) Plan Screening Requirement: Criminal Background Check Apply for this position « Openings at Transylvania University"
    },
    "https://www.transy.edu/employment-opportunities/#op-709985-mfa-venue-assistant-technical-coordinator": {
      "title": "MFA Venue Assistant Technical Coordinator",
      "description": "« Openings at Transylvania University MFA Venue Assistant Technical Coordinator Location: Lexington, Kentucky, United States Part-time Founded in 1780, Transylvania University is one of the nation’s oldest institutions, but don’t let our age fool you. Ranked in the Top 100 Best Liberal Arts colleges for 2025 by Niche, we’re a vibrant, forward-thinking campus in the heart of Lexington, Kentucky full of curious minds, creative energy, and people who genuinely love what they do. We are mentors, innovators and community builders who help shape the next generation of thinkers, creators and leaders. At Transylvania, we believe our people are our greatest strength. We seek enthusiasm, initiative, and a commitment to excellence to helping create a campus environment where students, faculty and staff thrive. As a member of our community, you’ll work alongside dedicated colleagues who value collaboration, innovative thinking and shared success. We invite applications for this opportunity to not only belong but belong to Team Transy! This is a year-round, part-time position averaging 25 hours per week. The schedule is made up of a combination of regularly scheduled and flexible hours, including nights and weekends, to support events. It is not benefit-eligible. What you’ll do:  Help to maintain the facilities and equipment of the Mitchell Fine Arts Center, with a focus on stage and performance-related areas.  Train and manage student and professional crews.  Mix audio, set/design lighting for events, operate fly systems, maintain organizational systems, and collaborate with various departments across campus.  Oversee and manage events in the Technical Coordinator's absence.  This role requires a high level of critical thinking with the ability to anticipate risks. This is a highly active and hands-on position, with approximately 80% of working time spent throughout the facility on projects or events, both with crews and independently. This includes working overhead at heights and in small spaces. What you bring:  Bachelor of Arts in Theater/related field or three years of experience in the live entertainment/ performance industry is required.  Ability to work with theatrical control systems.  Supplemental training and certifications such as specific control systems, rigging, basic first aid, diversity-equity-inclusion training, box office management, and other applicable certifications and education are desirable.  Ability to work independently while maintaining effective communication with the Technical Coordinator.  Exceptional verbal and written communication skills.  Ability to provide excellent customer service to students, faculty, and staff across campus. Why you’ll love belonging here:  A campus that feels alive, where every day brings new faces, new ideas, and the kind of energy that makes work feel meaningful.  A community that cares, with colleagues who celebrate wins, support challenges and make you feel part of something bigger.  A space to grow and shine, with professional development, leadership opportunities and a culture that encourages to bring your best ideas forward.  A setting that’s hard to beat, right in the heart of Lexington, Transylvania is walkable, welcoming and full of charm and history. How to apply: Please apply by visiting www.transy.edu/jobs. Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. An Equal Opportunity Employer M/F/D/V Apply for this position « Openings at Transylvania University"
    }
  },
